\ A quotation sits in the loop-invariant region below a `times` loop whose body
\ does not consume it, so it is carried unchanged across the back-edge and returned
\ as the word output. Without reification the carried quotation_body is skipped by
\ the loop's entry flush and later rewritten to a stale raw_at_slot; reifying it
\ before the loop header writes the slot once so the carried value survives every
\ iteration. Building interpreter-free proves the carried quotation's code_ptr was
\ attached, since the `call` at the use site has no interpreter to fall back to.
carry-quot: ( -- q ) [ [ 7 ] 3 [ ] times ] ;

carry-quot call .
